    "field": "Atmospheric chemistry and physics",
    "problem": "High uncertainty in the rate of regional ozone recovery in the Northern Hemisphere exists because the impact of dynamical changes, particularly the polar vortex shifting toward Eurasia and enhancing localized ozone loss, is not well understood, potentially delaying expected recovery timelines.",
    "method": "The paper uses Empirical Orthogonal Function (EOF) analysis on observed and modeled total column ozone, combined with chemistry-climate-model simulations, to identify and explain a Eurasia-North America dipole mode in ozone loss, which is attributed to a persistent shift of the Arctic polar vortex towards Eurasia.",
    "task": "This paper investigates the cause of enhanced stratospheric ozone loss over the Eurasian continent, attributing it to a persistent shift of the polar vortex and projecting its impact on future regional ozone recovery using chemistry-climate models.",
